# Source art fetched from the wiki by tools/fetch_map_data.py. Big, and only an
# *input* to the terrain build -- the small derived region under data/regions/
# is what the game reads, and that is committed. Nobody needs the 8182-pixel
# render to play.
data/wiki/*.webp
data/wiki/*.png

# data/regions/ is deliberately NOT ignored. The heightmap and masks are
# generated, reproducible and about 3 MB compressed, and they were left out on
# the reasoning that anything reproducible should be rebuilt rather than
# vendored. That is a rule for build *inputs*; applied to the game's own map it
# meant a fresh clone had no ground to stand on and would not run until the
# player installed numpy and ran two scripts. The scripts are how the map is
# *re*-made, not how it is obtained.

# Godot
.godot/
*.import
export_presets.cfg

# Test/diagnostic scratch
.test_home*/
.diag/
*.log

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
